    "q-129521": {
      "dom_id": "step-q129521",
      "name": "Question 1",
      "problem": "For two independent random variables $X$ and $Y,$ we have $\\text{Var}[X]=7$ and $\\text{Var}[Y]=9.$ Find $\\text{Var}[Y-X].$",
      "worked_solution": "Recall that if $X$ and $Y$ are independent random variables, then \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[Y\\pm X]=\\text{Var}[Y]+\\text{Var}[X].\n$$\n\nSubstituting the given data into the formula above, we obtain \n\n$$\n\\text{Var}[Y-X]=9+7=16.\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
